ExamVault — Interface Contract
Purpose: single source of truth for the three handoff points where bugs love to hide — Backend ↔ Contract ↔ Frontend. Every teammate fills in their section with real, final values once their track is working. Update this doc, don't just talk about it — it's what integration checks against.

1. Backend → Contract (encrypted file hash format)
Backend dev fills this in:
• Hash algorithm used: SHA-256 (confirm)
• Format returned by /api/paper/upload: (e.g. hex string with 0x prefix, or raw hex without prefix?)
• Example actual output: encryptedFileHash: "____________________"
• Length of the string: _____ characters

Contract dev fills this in:
• Expected type in registerPaper(): bytes32 (confirm)
• Does it need 0x prefix to convert cleanly from string → bytes32? Y / N
• Any conversion step needed before calling the contract (e.g. ethers.utils.hexlify / padding)?

⚠️ Known risk: SHA-256 produces a 32-byte hash — bytes32 expects exactly that, but string formatting (with/without 0x, upper/lowercase) can silently break the match. Test with one real value end-to-end before assuming this works.

2. Contract → Frontend (ABI + function signatures)
Contract dev fills this in:
• Deployed contract address (Sepolia): ____________________
• Final function signatures (copy exact from deployed contract):
   - registerPaper(________________)
   - isReleaseAllowed(________________)
   - logAccess(________________)
   - verifyHash(________________)
• Where's the ABI JSON file? (path or paste location)

Frontend dev fills this in:
• Contract address used in config: ____________________ (must match above exactly)
• ABI source used: (imported from file / pasted directly — where?)
• Confirmed function calls match signatures above: Y / N

⚠️ Known risk: if frontend's ABI is copied before the contract's final version, function names/param order can drift. Always re-copy ABI after any contract change.

3. Backend → Frontend (API request/response shapes)
Backend dev fills this in:
Endpoint	Method	Request body/params	Response shape
/api/paper/upload	POST	field names e.g. file, paperId, releaseTime, authorizedCenters	{ encryptedFileHash, wrappedKeys, paperId }
/api/paper/:paperId/release-key	GET	query params e.g. centerId	success shape + 403 error shape
/api/paper/:paperId/audit-log	GET	none / params	array shape, field names

Frontend dev fills this in:
• Confirmed form field names match backend's expected request body: Y / N
• Confirmed response parsing matches actual backend response keys: Y / N
• Backend base URL used in frontend config: ____________________

⚠️ Known risk: field name mismatches (paperId vs paper_id, file vs paperFile) are the #1 silent failure here — test with real curl/Postman calls, not just code review.

